From f3c655c21de3f63c173845a8baf8c3a9f9a184f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gogo <gogo@bluedynamics.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:36:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Keep frames within a time budget under heavy traffic

frame_budget: P (set to 90 by --fast) lets drawing, log parsing and
physics together use P% of each frame. Physics gets what is left; the
number of blobs that collide with each other adapts after every step to
fit (aiming at 70% of the physics budget for headroom). Which blobs
collide is random: 5% of them swap with passive blobs every frame, so
every blob gets its turn. Physics runs every frame in this mode, so no
frame is heavier than the others.

Also removes two causes of chokes:

- chipmunk: removing a shape scanned the whole contact set, per shape,
  and the Ruby wrapper scanned all bodies/shapes (calling == on each)
  per removal. Contacts of removed shapes are now dropped in one pass at
  the start of the next step, and the wrapper keeps identity hashes.
  Simulated at 3000 blobs/s with everything colliding: 88 -> 46 ms/frame.
- stdin: a burst of input was parsed in a single frame (100k lines with
  a 30 us parser: ~0.9 s frames). Parsing now stops after 4 ms per frame
  and continues next frame; reading pauses at a 4 MB backlog.

Requires bin/setup to rebuild the vendored chipmunk.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
